<title>UK: UK new construction orders rise 8.0% 3mths to Jan.</title>
<headline>UK new construction orders rise 8.0% 3mths to Jan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK new construction orders were up 8.0 percent in the three months to January versus the previous three months but the volume of total new orders fell in January alone, the Department of the Environment said.  </p>
<p>Total orders were one percent lower in the three months to January compared with the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>			  3/mth vs 3/mth	3/mth vs yr earlier</p>
<p>    Total		    +8			 -1</p>
<p>    Private housing     +13			+40</p>
<p>    Infrastructure	 +9			+19</p>
<p>    Public non-housing  -20			-36</p>
<p>    Private industrial  +17			 -3</p>
<p>    Private commercial  +18			-16</p>
<p>In current prices, the total value of new orders in January alone was 1.985 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
